        userPersonas: {
          id: 'user-personas',
          title: '🧭 Who Should Use What: Personas and Recommendations',
          items: [
            '**Beginner (no local LLM experience):** [LM Studio](/local-llms/how-to-install-lm-studio) + Qwen2.5-Coder 7B -- GUI, no terminal needed, includes FIM for code completion.',
            '**Laptop developer (8–16 GB RAM, everyday coding):** Ollama + Qwen2.5-Coder 7B or DeepSeek-Coder V2 Lite -- balanced quality and performance, runs smoothly for hours.',
            '**Advanced developer (debugging, refactoring, complex reasoning):** Ollama + Qwen2.5-Coder 32B -- highest HumanEval (87%), handles multi-file context and algorithm design.',
            '**IDE-first workflow (VS Code, Cursor, JetBrains):** Continue.dev + Starcoder2 15B -- FIM-optimized for in-editor code completion at cursor position.',
            '**Privacy-critical environments (GDPR, HIPAA, proprietary code):** Any model above via Ollama -- zero external API calls, 100% on-premises, code never leaves your machine.',
          ],
          callouts: [
            { type: 'warning', text: '❌ **Avoid:** Running Qwen2.5-Coder 32B on machines with <20 GB free RAM. Latency becomes unusable (1–3 tokens/sec). Either use Qwen2.5-Coder 7B or DeepSeek-Coder V2 Lite on smaller machines.' },
            { type: 'warning', text: '❌ **Avoid:** Using general-purpose models (Llama 3.1 8B) when you need IDE autocomplete. Only code-specific models with FIM support work for in-editor completion -- Qwen2.5-Coder, DeepSeek-Coder, or Starcoder2.' },
            { type: 'insight', text: 'Beginner → intermediate → advanced is also a progression in hardware requirements. Start with 7B (8 GB), upgrade to 16B (16 GB) as you add tools and workflows, graduate to 32B (20+ GB) only if you need maximum reasoning quality.' },
          ],
        },
        whenNotToUse: {
          id: 'when-not-to-use',
          title: '❌ When NOT to Use Local LLMs for Coding',
          items: [
            '**You need latest framework knowledge (2025+ APIs):** Local models are trained on fixed cutoff dates. Qwen2.5-Coder trained through Q3 2024, DeepSeek-Coder through mid-2024. For Vue 3.5, Next.js 15, or Python 3.13 APIs released after model training, use GPT-5.5 or Claude 3.5 Sonnet (2024) which are constantly updated.',
            '**You need multi-file reasoning across large codebases (100k+ tokens):** Local models degrade on very long context. Latency becomes prohibitive. Cloud models (GPT-5.5, Claude) handle 100k+ token contexts natively. For architectural refactoring of entire services, use cloud models.',
            '**Latency must be <300ms (real-time interactive coding):** Local models run at 15-25 tokens/sec on CPU (typical laptops), producing a 5-10 second delay per response. GitHub Copilot and Claude in IDE complete suggestions in <1 second. For keystroke-level autocomplete, local models are too slow.',
            '**You need best-in-class debugging accuracy:** On complex debugging tasks (tracing multiple function call stacks, identifying subtle type errors), GPT-5.5 and Claude 3.5 Sonnet (2024) score 15-20% higher than local models on real-world code issues. Local models excel at generation; frontier models excel at diagnosis.',
            '**You cannot tolerate hallucination in generated code:** Local 7B models generate syntactically valid but logically incorrect code at ~2% rate on complex tasks. Cloud models hallucinate at <0.5% rate. For mission-critical code (payment systems, security), require human review or use frontier APIs.',
          ],
          callouts: [
            { type: 'insight', text: '👉 **Local LLMs are best for:** Privacy + offline work + cost control — NOT for peak performance. If maximum accuracy matters more than these three factors, use cloud APIs.' },
          ],
        },
