      seoTitle: 'Q4_K_M Quantization 2026: GGUF & Offloading Explained',
      intro: 'Complete guide to LLM quantization (Q4_K_M, Q5_K_M, Q8_0, GGUF) plus advanced VRAM reduction techniques: CPU offloading and multi-GPU layer splitting. Learn how to run Llama 3.3 70B on RTX 4090 via offloading, 2× RTX 4090 via layer splitting, or Mac Studio M2 Ultra natively. As of April 2026, combining techniques enables enterprise-scale local inference.',
      metaDescription: 'Q4_K_M reduces 70B model VRAM to 24GB. Learn GGUF quantization (Q4 vs Q5 vs Q8), CPU offloading, layer splitting, and how to run Llama 3.3 70B on RTX 4090.',
      publishDate: '2026-04-04',
      leadAnswerBlock: '**LLM quantization reduces model weight precision from 32-bit or 16-bit floats to 4-bit or 8-bit integers, cutting RAM requirements by 50-75% with minimal quality loss. Offloading and layer splitting extend these techniques beyond single-GPU constraints.**',
