      seoTitle: 'Multi-GPU Local LLMs 2026: Dual RTX 4090 for 70B at 100 tok/s',
      intro: 'Using multiple GPUs lets you run 70B+ models that don\'t fit in a single GPU\'s VRAM. Dual RTX 4090s (48 GB combined) run Llama 3.3 70B at Q4 at ~100 tok/sec — only 5–10% slower than a theoretical single 48 GB GPU due to inter-GPU communication overhead. As of April 2026, vLLM (tensor parallelism) and Ollama (automatic layer splitting) both support multi-GPU out of the box. NVLink reduces overhead to 3–5% but is unavailable on consumer RTX cards — PCIe 4.0/5.0 is sufficient for most dual-GPU setups.',
      metaDescription: '2× RTX 4090 (48 GB combined): Llama 3.3 70B at 100 tok/sec for $3,600. Only 5–10% speed penalty vs theoretical single GPU. vLLM tensor parallelism + Ollama auto-split. NVLink vs PCIe compared.',
